From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:09:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] perf(canvas): only the frames in view go live

A frame got its live document when it came within half a viewport of the
view, and kept it out to a whole viewport. The margin dates from when a
frame without a document was a blurred thumbnail and a booting one a white
flash: a short pan was to find documents waiting. Since then a frame
without its document shows a picture of itself at the sharpness of the
screen, and keeps it until the document has painted, so the swap is not
seen and the margin only decides how many documents boot off screen. At
60% on a 188-frame page of desktop screens that was 12 documents at every
rest of the camera, with 4 to 6 of them on screen. Each is a FrameView
mounted on the editor's main thread and a document started in the frames'
process, which they all share.

The entry margin is now a tenth of a viewport and the keep margin half of
one. The pictures keep the wider margin (SHARP_MARGIN, half a viewport), so
what a pan brings into view is already crisp.

perf/bench.mjs, old margins against new on one build, four interleaved
runs on a loaded machine, medians: live documents at 60% 12 -> 4-6;
leaving a neighbourhood and coming back, editor main thread 435 -> 183 ms
and every frame on screen showing its document after 602 -> 329 ms. The
other gestures are unchanged within the noise.

What it costs: a frame that has just scrolled into view is its picture
until the camera rests (120 ms), where it used to be a document already
if it had been within half a viewport. A press on it wakes it at once, as
on any frame showing its picture.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
